<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Then another promise followed</l><l>David’s seed upon the throne:</l><l>“I’ll rebuild His tabernacle</l><l>And by this I will be known.”</l><l>Lord, we thank Thee, Thou art faithful</l><l>To perform Thy promised word.</l><l>David’s tabernacle, ruined,</l><l>Soon by Thee will be restored.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Lord, we are that tabernacle,</l><l>Thy rebuilding work on earth;</l><l>Lord, restore Thyself a dwelling</l><l>Where is seen Thy boundless worth.</l><l>Thus shall all of mankind seek Thee.</l><l>And the Gentiles call Thy name.</l><l>From Thy holy tabernacle</l><l>All the earth shall know Thy fame.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Hasten, Lord, Thy work upon us</l><l>To restore and build us now.</l><l>For this work we give ourselves, Lord;</l><l>Here to Thee we make a vow:</l><l>“Though our strength is weak and feeble,</l><l>Yet our hearts would ever be</l><l>From this day, Lord, for Thy building,</l><l>Now and for eternity.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
